/T (The Expense Tracker is a console-based application that records daily expenses, keeps them in a linked list, sorts them by amount, searches for an amount quickly and lets the user undo the last entry. It is a beginner-level Data Structures and Algorithms \(DSA\) project built with core Java. )
/E (The Expense Tracker is a console-based application that records daily expenses, keeps them in a linked list, sorts them by amount, searches for an amount quickly and lets the user undo the last entry. It is a beginner-level Data Structures and Algorithms \(DSA\) project built with core Java. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
100 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 69 0 R
/T (A singly linked list, written from scratch with head and tail references, stores the expenses. An insertion sort on the list nodes arranges the expenses by amount from low to high, and Binary Search finds an expense by its amount once the data is sorted. A stack remembers the IDs of the added expenses so that the last addition can be undone. File handling saves the expenses to a text file when the program exits and loads them again when it starts. )
/E (A singly linked list, written from scratch with head and tail references, stores the expenses. An insertion sort on the list nodes arranges the expenses by amount from low to high, and Binary Search finds an expense by its amount once the data is sorted. A stack remembers the IDs of the added expenses so that the last addition can be undone. File handling saves the expenses to a text file when the program exits and loads them again when it starts. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
