/P 69 0 R
/E (Keeping track of daily expenses is a routine task for students and families. Writing them in a notebook is slow, the entries are easy to lose, and finding or comparing amounts takes time. A computer program can store every expense, sort the amounts and find any entry within moments. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
104 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 69 0 R
/E (This project demonstrates the idea on a small scale. The user adds an expense by entering a category and an amount, and the program gives it a unique ID such as X101. The expenses are kept in a linked list, which can be viewed, sorted by amount and searched with Binary Search. The last added expense can be undone, and all data is saved to a file so that it is available the next time the program runs. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
