175 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (sortByAmount\(\) builds a new sorted list. Each node is taken from the old list and inserted at its correct place by amount. Equal amounts are placed after earlier ones, so the sort is stable. head and tail are then updated and sorted is set to true. binarySearch\(\) sorts the list if needed, copies the nodes into an array and applies Binary Search on the amount. On a match it keeps searching the left half to return the first matching expense. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
176 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (undoLast\(\) pops the latest ID from the stack, finds that node in the list, removes it by changing the previous node's link, updates the tail if required and reduces size. loadFromFile\(\) reads each line of expenses.txt \(ID, category, amount separated by commas\) with BufferedReader, skips wrong lines and adds the valid expenses to the list. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
