/Title (A singly linked list, written from scratch with head and tail references, stores the expenses. An insertion sort on the list nodes arranges the expenses by amount from low to high, and Binary Search finds an expense by its amount once the data is sorted. A stack remembers the IDs of the added expenses so that the last addition can be undone. File handling saves the expenses to a text file when the program exits and loads them again when it starts.)
